 "result": "The failing call is at `src/tessel/sessions.py:374`, in `persist_session`:\n\n```python\nresponse.set_cookie(\n    name,\n    val,\n    expires=expires,\n    httponly=httponly,\n    domain=domain,\n    path=path,\n    secure=secure,\n    partitioned=partitioned,\n    samesite=samesite,\n)\n```\n\nThe rejected argument is `partitioned=partitioned`, from `partitioned = self.get_cookie_partitioned(app)`. Werkzeug 3.0.3's `Response.set_cookie()` has no such keyword, hence `TypeError: Response.set_cookie() got an unexpected keyword argument 'partitioned'`.\n\nThe `delete_cookie(...)` call earlier in the same function passes `partitioned=` too. I haven't confirmed whether 3.0.3 also rejects it there, since the tests I ran only hit the `set_cookie` path.",
